WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.262
BTRIM is excellent for boundary whitespace.

00:00:03.262 --> 00:00:06.797
It removes spaces from the start and end of a string.

00:00:06.797 --> 00:00:11.252
But it does not collapse repeated spaces inside the value.

00:00:11.252 --> 00:00:13.567
That distinction is important.

00:00:13.567 --> 00:00:22.747
If you need to normalize internal whitespace, you need a different function such as REGEXP_REPLACE with a

00:00:22.747 --> 00:00:27.502
repeated-whitespace pattern. Text cleaning should separate normalization from interpretation.

00:00:27.502 --> 00:00:33.817
Trimming spaces or standardizing case is usually safe when the rule is documented;

00:00:33.817 --> 00:00:40.047
correcting a person's name or guessing an email address is a much stronger intervention.

00:00:40.047 --> 00:00:43.979
Preserve the original value when auditability matters.
